y in school. Chieko Shirakaba is the rich snob with the two yes-girls who always take her side. There is a bookworm, a mystic, a scientist, and a pop singer. All of these are true to their descriptions: the mystic is always foretelling doom via tarot cards, spirits, or some other occult technique. The pop singer never says anything except as a song. The bookworm always has her nose in a book. These eccentricities add to the series' humor.\n\n(Source: Anime News Network)"},"tags":[{"name":"Robots","rank":80,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Female Protagonist","rank":79,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Urban","rank":79,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Reincarnation","rank":79,"spoiler":true},{"name":"Episodic","rank":79,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Nekomimi","rank":73,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Slapstick","rank":66,"spoiler":false},{"name":"School","rank":50,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Ojou-sama","rank":30,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Idol","rank":30,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Musical Theater","rank":20,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Parody","rank":20,"spoiler":false}],"titles":{"display":"All Purpose Cultural Cat Girl Nuku Nuku TV","english":"All Purpose Cultural Cat Girl Nuku Nuku TV","native":"万能文化猫娘","romaji":"Bannou Bunka Neko-Musume (1998)","synonyms":[{"language":"zh","source":"bangumi","value":"万能文化猫娘 TV"},{"language":null,"source":"bangumi","value":"万能文化猫娘・TV版"}]},"trailer":null,"visibility":"general"}